  "claims": [
    "A finite rule/reference certificate checker rejects invalid arity, forward references, and premise mismatches. Acceptance implies an inhabitant in every proof-relevant model of the presentation.",
    "A shared numerical evaluator commutes with algebra homomorphisms. Its expandedSize is exactly the node count of tree expansion, without needing to materialize that tree.",
    "One retained-state adaptive MAC local comparison has two interpretations of exactly the same certificate: geometric Cells and ordinary conditional-kernel/loss equality proofs. An explicit model homomorphism erases the former to the latter.",
    "For the deliberately duplicated stress family at repetition level k, all certificates are accepted. Node count is k+3, reference count is 2*k+3, and expanded tree node count is 5*2^k-1.",
    "Successful linked-list reference traversals in the exhibited family total k^2+5*k+4. Linear node count is not reported as a linear checking-time theorem.",
    "A one-node reflexivity certificate is accepted at the same final boundary in both models; the stress-family expansion is not a minimum-proof lower bound."
  ],
