  "scope": [
    "The MAC attack, secret/oracle state, trace, and existing 1/256 statistical bound are reused from the previous retained-state model; no new game bound or native execution result.",
    "The experiment uses one checked local MAC comparison and deliberate repetition. It is a sharing control, not evidence that actual full cryptographic proofs require exponentially large trees.",
    "The one-node alternative makes the final repeated-comparison boundary trivial in both models. No minimum-proof or higher-dimensional size lower-bound separation.",
    "Ordinary semantic proofs are a concrete shared-lemma baseline in this grammar, not a benchmark of external frameworks or all possible proof systems.",
    "The finite generic checker validates inference-reference data, not conditional requirements or model soundness itself. Those are supplied by separately checked models; condition extraction/repair costs are outside this benchmark.",
    "The generic rule type need not admit a finite encoding; actual byte results are only for the explicitly finite Rule/Bool/Nat experiment and its chosen renderer.",
    "No automatic hash-consing or translation of arbitrary generated Cell syntax into a globally shared proof graph is implemented this turn. Full decoder, kernel-checking measurements, library-inclusive size, and repair benchmarks remain open.",
    "Full mixed finite higher basis including copy/discard, and publication novelty, remain open."
  ],
